# Move the arm to a pose, or to a named configuration.
#
# The goal is in task space, never joint space. A joint-space goal leaks the
# robot's kinematics upward and breaks every promise L3 makes — swapping an
# xArm 5 for a 7-DOF arm must change nothing above this line.

geometry_msgs/PoseStamped target        # in any frame TF can resolve
string named_configuration              # alternative to `target`, e.g. "home";
                                        # exactly one of the two must be set
float64 velocity_scaling                # 0..1 of the arm's configured limit
float64 acceleration_scaling            # 0..1
bool cartesian_path                     # follow a straight line rather than a
                                        # planned joint path
---
ResultCode result
geometry_msgs/PoseStamped reached       # where the tool actually ended up
float64 position_error_m                # m, between `reached` and `target`
builtin_interfaces/Duration duration
---
float64 fraction_complete               # 0..1
geometry_msgs/PoseStamped current
float64 distance_remaining_m            # m
